zoox,2025-06,46024,287293,215216,431444,34265,69540,1,1,1,1,1,1,2026-10-15,"US est. (rebuilt 2026-10-03, smoothed 2026-11-02, one path 2026-11-03): the month's California driverless miles (CA DMV, permit AVDT004) plus a Las Vegas share at one rate a Las Vegas driving day each month, the rates taking the smoothest path, the least sum of squared month-to-month changes in their logarithm from May 2025 on, that keeps all four of Zoox's statements within their ranges, the lifetime counting the 40,080 earlier driverless miles: the 1M mark crossed during Dec 1-7, since Fortune, reporting what Zoox's CTO said on Monday, Dec 8, wrote that 'Zoox crossed the 1 million mile technical threshold for autonomous rides just last week' (Fortune, Dec 8, 2025); 'approximately 1.3 million' at Dec 31 (letter to NHTSA, Jan 28, 2026, docket NHTSA-2025-0523-0004 p.22) read as 1.25M-1.35M; 'nearly two million autonomous miles' (Mar 23-24, 2026) at Mar 24 read as 1.88M-2.00M; and 'over 3 million miles on public roads' (Bloomberg, Aug 5, 2026; 'more than 3 million' in the Las Vegas Sun, Aug 6) at Aug 5 read as 3.00M-3.20M. Two of them bind: the path crosses 1M at the start of Dec 1 and stands at 1.25M on Dec 31. The Las Vegas share runs 784, 1,246, 1,934, 2,898, 4,123 and 5,435 miles a day June-November. Band: California plus half to twice the Las Vegas share, as for the earlier rows, within what the statements allow; November's cumulative band, 835,274 to 969,873, is the crossing's own: 1M not before Dec 1 and by the end of Dec 7, less the earlier miles at their own band ([data/README.md, Zoox anchors](data/#zoox-anchors))."
