zoox,2025-12,250001,1209920,1190013,1319873,250000,454739,1,1,1,1,1,1,2026-10-15,"US est. (rebuilt 2026-10-03, smoothed 2026-11-02, one path 2026-11-03): the cumulative is the low end of Zoox's 'approximately 1.3 million driverless autonomous miles' at Dec 31, 2025 (letter to NHTSA, Jan 28, 2026, docket NHTSA-2025-0523-0004 p.22), read as 1.25M-1.35M, where the smoothest path through Zoox's statements puts it (the June-November rows): 1.25M less the 40,080 pre-series miles, 1,209,920. Its band, 1,190,013 to 1,319,873, is that statement's range less the pre-series miles at their own band; later months' bands chain from it. December's miles are at least 250,000, the 1.25M of Dec 31 less the 1M not reached before Dec 1, and the path puts them there (250,001 with the earlier months' rounding): 6,500.65 Las Vegas miles a day, the rate it holds from then on. California's December, in no DMV report yet, is estimated from CPUC's December/November ratio ([data/README.md, Zoox anchors](data/#zoox-anchors))."
zoox,2026-01,210000,1419920,1353013,1589873,163000,270000,1,1,1,1,1,1,2026-10-15,"US est. (rebuilt 2026-10-27, one path 2026-11-03): California is CPUC's driverless miles x 1.19 for the DMV-reported miles CPUC misses (an assumption, the midpoint of 1.05-1.33); the rest, mostly Las Vegas, follows the smoothest path through Zoox's four statements (the June-November 2025 rows), which holds December 2025's 6,500.65 miles a Las Vegas driving day on: no later statement binds it, and it puts 1,887,653 lifetime miles at Mar 24, inside 'nearly two million autonomous miles' (Mar 23-24, 2026) read as 1.88M-2.00M. January leaves out Jan 22-26, when Las Vegas passenger service was down (LVRJ, Jan 28, 2026, dating it from an X user's posts). Bands: statement rounding, drift from the midpoint of Jan 1-Mar 24 and month noise ([data/README.md, Ghost months](data/#ghost-months); [data/README.md, Zoox anchors](data/#zoox-anchors))."
