zoox,2026-03,260000,1909920,1861485,2123912,200000,337000,1,1,1,1,1,1,2026-10-15,"US est. (rebuilt 2026-10-27, one path 2026-11-03): March at the smooth path's 6,500.65 Las Vegas miles a day, as every 2026 month, which puts 1,887,653 lifetime miles at Mar 24. Cumulative band 1,861,485 to 2,123,912: 'nearly two million' read as 1.88M-2.00M as of Mar 17-24, less the pre-series miles at their own band, carried to Mar 31. It counts driverless miles: Zoox's Mar 23 post puts them 'in our robotaxi', apart from 'our retrofitted testing fleet', and with California's 1,213,646 safety-driver test miles of Dec 2024-Nov 2025 alone, a count including those would have passed 2.5M by Dec 31, 2025 ([data/README.md, Zoox anchors](data/#zoox-anchors))."
zoox,2026-04,250000,2159920,2051485,2452912,190000,329000,1,1,1,1,1,1,2026-10-15,"US est. (rebuilt 2026-10-27, one path 2026-11-03): California is CPUC's driverless miles x 1.19 (filed through September; July and August in the [CPUC Q3 driverless pilot report (ZIP)](https://www.cpuc.ca.gov/-/media/cpuc-website/divisions/consumer-protection-and-enforcement-division/documents/tlab/av-programs/av-pilot-2026q3.zip)); the rest, mostly Las Vegas, follows the smoothest path through Zoox's four statements, flat at 6,500.65 a day from December 2025 (no fleet count since ~65 Las Vegas vehicles in service on Sep 2; no pause, recall or halt found). It puts 3,083,678 lifetime miles at Aug 5, inside 'more than 3 million miles on public roads' (Aug 5; Bloomberg, Las Vegas Sun) read as 3.00M-3.20M. End-July cumulative floor 2,880,077: 'more than 3 million' as of Jul 29-Aug 5, less the pre-series miles' high edge; 'more than' sets no ceiling. Bands: statement rounding, drift from the midpoint of Mar 25-Aug 5 and month noise ([data/README.md, Ghost months](data/#ghost-months); [data/README.md, Zoox anchors](data/#zoox-anchors))."
