waymo,2021-07,36101,36101,19583,62196,19583,62196,1,1,1,1,1,1,2026-10-15,"US est.: Waymo's rider-only miles by calendar year (Kusano et al. 2025, Table 2, from its Safety Impact hub: 328,000 in 2021, 524,000 in 2022) and its first million rider-only miles on Jan 21, 2023 (Waymo's one-million-mile paper), spread over the months with daily rates interpolated linearly between those totals; January 2023 keeps Jan 1-21's daily rate for the whole month. The series starts in July 2021, so the miles driven before it, 205,000 (range 150,000-260,000), come off; July-December 2021's bands and every cumulative band carry that range, and each month's band an allowance for the monthly split, half to twice a month's miles in 2022 ([data/README.md, Waymo anchors](data/#waymo-anchors); [data/README.md, Waymo monthly allocation](data/#waymo-monthly-allocation))."
